1
00:00:00,952 --> 00:00:07,372
(Sheldon:)Leonard, what you're experiencing
is a classic Jungian crisis...

2
00:00:07,542 --> 00:00:10,582
(Sheldon:)...in which the aging individual
mourns the loss...

3
00:00:10,754 --> 00:00:13,884
...of the never-to-be-realized
ideal family unit.

4
00:00:14,174 --> 00:00:17,554
(Leonard:)-Thank you, that's very comforting.
-That's not the comforting part.

5
00:00:18,511 --> 00:00:21,431
(Leonard:)-It's not?
-No. No, the comforting part...

6
00:00:21,598 --> 00:00:26,558
(Sheldon:)...is that the Germans have a term
for what you're feeling, "Weltschmerz."

7
00:00:27,145 --> 00:00:31,525
(Sheldon:)It means the depression that arises
from comparing the world as it is...

8
00:00:31,691 --> 00:00:35,111
(Sheldon:)...to a hypothetical idealized world.

9
00:00:35,487 --> 00:00:37,737
(Leonard:)You're right, I do feel better.

10
00:00:37,906 --> 00:00:41,576
Yeah, the Germans have always been
a comforting people.

11
00:00:44,245 --> 00:00:48,545
(Sheldon:)Just remember, Leonard, where
your biological family has failed you...

12
00:00:48,708 --> 00:00:51,878
(Sheldon:)...you always have me,
your surrogate family.

13
00:00:54,255 --> 00:00:56,005
(Leonard:)You're my surrogate family?

14
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:03,020
(Sheldon:)If it's any consolation,
I'm not happy about it either. Good night.

